  "question": {
    "text": "A person travels <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> distance with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> distance with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in the same direction. The average velocity of the person is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, then the relation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will be",
    "image": null
  },
